<title>USA: Williams-Sonoma Inc Q3 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Williams-Sonoma Inc Q3 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>($ in thousands except per share figures)</p>
<p>				   13 Wks    13 Wks   39 Wks   39 Wks</p>
<p>				   Ended	Ended    Ended    Ended</p>
<p>				Oct. 27,   Oct. 29, Oct. 27, Oct. 29,</p>
<p>				     1996     1995	1996     1995</p>
<p> Net sales		    171,154   138,363  484,050  384,256</p>
<p> Operating profit (loss)    1,715   (4,535)    (441)  (5,254)</p>
<p> Interest expense	     1,317     1,695    4,334    2,932</p>
<p> Pre-tax earnings (loss)	398   (6,230)  (4,775)  (8,186)</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss)	    231   (3,669)  (2,770)  (4,809)</p>
<p>Average number of shares outstanding (000s):</p>
<p>  Primary		   26,453  25,378(a) 25,453(a) 25,354(a)</p>
<p>  Fully diluted	 26,511(b) 25,378(a) 25,453(a) 25,354(a)</p>
<p>Earnings (loss) per share:</p>
<p>  Primary &amp; fully diluted    0.01    (0.14)   (0.11)   (0.19)</p>
<p>(a) Incremental shares from assumed exercise of stock options and convertible debt are antidilutive for primary and fully diluted loss per share. (b) Incremental shares from conversion of convertible debt are antidilutive for fully diluted earnings per share. Same store sales for Q3 1996 rose 4.4 pct. Mail order sales rose 11.4 pct.</p>
</text>
